On Tue, Oct 13, 1998 at 10:29:13AM -0300, Jay.Estabrook@digital.com wrote:
> Think about what "ps" (and "top" and "vmstat", among others) might be
> attempting to do - access kernel data structures via /dev/kmem.

They do no such thing, and never have (on alpha).  All three of those
programs get their data from /proc.


> I believe the same type of Oops happens frequently with "top" on Alpha SMP
> systems under heavy load. It's all a bit frustrating, because "top" and
> "vmstat" are such useful tools to see what's going on in one's system... :-\

At one time there was a bug in thread_saved_pc, the fix for which
is in current kernels.  Prove to me that a `cat /proc/*/stat' can
still crash under load and I'll look again.


