When it finally finished, I have a weird, small file called vmlinux.lds in
the /usr/src/linux/arch/alpha dir.  The same file is in all the other arch
dir's.  Is there something I need to do special before running make boot to
tell it this is an alpha or something?

I boot off of a floppy from an SRM (>>>) prompt.  I need to create a kernel,
put it on a floppy and then make that floppy bootable.  I've never worked on
an alpha before, and making the kernel small enough to put on a floppy is
also worrying me.

HELP ME!!!  This thing is driving me crazy.  I've tried for or five
different kernel's and just can't seem to make it work.  What am I
missing??!!

Thanks for all the help.

Regards,

