I posted this a couple of days ago. i recently purchased two AS200/233's. I
had a lot of trouble, but eventually discovered that everything you need is
on the RH disk, its just that the instructions are not correct, and some
files are different.

1. Update to the _8 version of ARC from Digital. It is available under the
"latest' directory.

2. Format a dos floppy and copy (under dos) linload and the avanti milo image
to the floppy. (Rename avanti => milo) Don't use rawrite as shown in the
addendum.

3. Use rawrite to make the bootimage and ramdisk. For the bootimage, don't
use the xl file as instructed in the manual; it won't work with the scsi and
will turn it off. Instead use the file named avanti.img in the images file.

Doing this, the installation was flawless and the system seems to work
perfectly.

All the docs on the BB mentioned vary from a little to a lot more complicated
than this. I think RH has all the right pieces there, they just don't seem to
have the directions correct. I am surprised they haven't put a note in their
errata about this. This has to be the predominant platform for Alpha Linux
installation right now.


