I went to work this morning confident that my Alpha was running fine - It's
been up 25 days since the last reboot, I haven't seen the syslogd problem, and
everything is rosy.  I get to work and I can't telnet back into the box.  I
telnet to my firewall machine (an Intel Linux box) and it can't even ping the
alpha on the local net.  I can ping my wife's mac just fine.  Fearing the
worst, I come home to find the box running happily, but it can't ping
anything, not even itself (192.168.1.1).  It can ping localhost, of course.
The green lights on the hub are all on.  So I tried an "ifdown eth0; ifup
eth0" and it worked.  Now I can reach everywhere, mail and news are flowing
again.  I'm happy.

Very strange.

-- 
Paul Tomblin, ptomblin@xcski.com.
