Adam Jacobs <ajk@socrates.berkeley.edu> wrote:
> 
> Hi folks,
> I'm trying to install RH 5.1 on a new Alphastation 200 4/233 (webauction).
> I'm using an old Quantum disk and an external CD-ROM (actually CD-R burner)
> which the SRM firmware recognizes just fine ('show device').  I boot
> MILO off a floppy from the SRM all right, but as soon as I try an 'ls'
> (the disk has an ext2 fs on it from my multia) or even just a 'show',
> when MILO initializes its devices, it hangs before scanning the SCSI bus.
> 
> ncr53c8xx : at PCI bus 0, device 6, function 0
> ncr_attach: unit=0 chip=810 base=2001000, io_port=8800, irq=11
> ncr53c810-0: assuming 40MHz clock          ( <--- could THIS be the problem?)
> ncr53c810-0: initial value of SCNTL3 = 03, final = 13
> ncr53c810-0: requesting shared irq 11 (dev_id=0xfffffc000003e090)
> ncr53c810-0: restart (scsi_reset).
> scsi0 : ncr53c8xx (rel 1.12d)
> scsi : 1 host.
> 
> And there it just hangs forever (although once or twice it repeated
> something like restart (ncr dead?) over and over, and ONCE only it managed
> to recognize the two devices on the bus before going into the 
> restart (ncr dead?) loop.
> 
> I think I've checked all the obvious things I could be doing wrong.
> To wit:
> 
> 	- it doesn't seem to be a termination problem or to be related
> 	  to the devices on the bus.  The same thing happens even if
> 	  I disconnect the disk, the CD, or both (adding termination as
> 	  appropriate), and the same thing happens with other disks I've
> 	  tried.  I tried both auto-sensing and required termination
> 	  (jumper 21) of the external SCSI.  Anyway, SRM has no trouble
> 	  recognizing the devices on the bus.
> 
> 	- I'm using the latest stable MILO from gatekeeper, namely
> 
> /pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Miniloader/latest-Images/Alphastation 200/milo.dd 
> 
> 	But I've also tried the REALLY new ones in
> 
> /pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-981008/avanti 
> 	and
> /pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/avanti
>         and also
> /pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-avanti-980606
> 	
> 	all to no avail. 
> 
> Since the same thing happens with all the MILOs (mili?) I've tried,
> and since other people have manifestly been able to install Linux on
> their AS200's with those same MILOs, I'm beginning to wonder if I have
> a hardware problem.  On the other hand the fact that SRM scans the bus
> successfully is reassuring.  But maybe someone else has seen this problem 
> and knows the cure?
> 
> Thanks,
> Adam Jacobs
> ajk@garnet.berkeley.edu
