Hi Adam,

	I have a suggestion: try some of the diagnostic commands in the SRM
console.  There are some (advanced) diagnostic commands available that are
not covered in the SRM-HOWTO or the user's manual.  They may help you to
determine where the problem is occuring.  Here is the URL for the document:

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/info/semiconductor/literature/srmcons.pdf.

I believe you're looking for Chapter 4, commands "exer" and "test".  I have
used them before on my AS200 so I cannot garauntee their existance in your
firmware.  Let us know how it works.

Thanks to those who responded to my "SRM unplugged" post a while back,
where I obtained this information.

Good luck,
-bp
