On Fri, Oct 23, 1998 at 04:13:12PM +0200, Roman Martonak wrote:

> Is this version able to play directly from URL ?

Nope. But inserting 

   setbuf(myfile, 0);

after line 223 in httpget.c (after the fdopen, just before relocate = FALSE)
makes it work for me.

The reason is that mpg123 mixes buffered (fgets) and unbuffered (read)
calls on the network sockets which causes it to "miss" the beginning of
the MP3 -> you only hear garbage. The fix just makes it use no buffer in
any way; there would probably be better ways to do this.

I mailed this to the author of mpg123 a couple of weeks ago (when I needed
a mpg123 that could play from URLs :) ) but never got a reply.

