With regards to your message at 01:10 PM 10-23-98 -0400, Keith Baker. Where
you stated:
>Unless I am missing some mail I have asked about this driver.  Does it
>support the udb scsi card?  and if so, the default 20mhz...  is the udb
>card capable of that?
>
The onboard SCSI on the UDB is a 53C810.
It does SCSI-2 fast, narrow, which is 10MHz clock. It has a maximum data
transfer rate of 10MB/sec. It is an 8-bit SCSI device.
It does NOT do wide SCSI, UltraSCSI ( 20MHz) or Ultra2 SCSI (Low Voltage
Differential).

The current Symbios drivers from ftp://ftp.tux.org/pub/roudier/ are what is
needed for success with this chip, and the entire 53c8xx family.

Use these, not the 53c7xx drivers.



