And a version of its driver is ... ????

> Does anyone know what
> causes this and is there a way to force the fast scsi.

53c8xx driver comes with a pretty long (mine current one is 58949 bytes
long) README.ncr53c8xx file in drivers/scsi source subdirectory
which describes how to set up various parameters and why you would want,
or would not, to do that.  The current driver versions are better
in detecting hardware capabilities and also provide more flexible
interface for overriding/changing various settings.  In particular
you can do that from a boot line on a device-by-device basis.
