> curious if anyone else out there has done this with their alpha box, and if
> so, what terminal program are you using?

I use XWin32. Basically, run xdm and use X-win32 in single-window mode
with a XDMCP broadcast. Works great for me. Also, try SuperX by Frontier
Technologies. It's faster, more stable sometimes, and doesn't have the
enforced per-conncurrent-use licensing. I'm using the 30-day trial I got
from winfiles.com.  

I used to use xwin with rexec, in multi window mode, and simply called
"xterm -display $myip:0.0" on the other end.

I'm using redhat 4.2, 5.0 and 5.1, alpha and i386

> 

> Also, I'm not sure what has to be done server side to get this started.  Any
> hints would be greatly appreciated.  Thank-you for any help.
> 

As I said, run XDM. it's really easy that way.

you can also etst with Xnest:

	Xnest -query linuxbox.foo.net

under X. It works great for me, YMMV

Rick



