Noah I Rosenberg wrote:


Noah,

The parts of the error message about Data CRC error  message reference sectors
and blocks on the Floppy drive which are not accessible.

Inaccessibility of the sectors could be the result of bad floppies, but you
say that they can be read on other machines and that the disks are good.

You may have drive head alignment problems.  You may wish to contack DEC to
see about drive replacements.  The part number is VX40N-AA.   You may also
wish to contact other specialized vendors of these type products, like
Starship Computers in Durham, New Hampshire.  They may be able to help.

Of course, if you have the expertise, you could try aligning the heads
yourself, but you need specialized equipment to that, plus the know how.  I
think that the drive is originally a Citizen brand or an NEC, but could be
wrong.  I haven't seen it in at least a couple of years.

S Computers, at 35 Mitchel Road,
Lee (Durham), New Hamp  03824

might be a good place to start.  I bought my Multia from them new several
years ago, and I was extremely pleased with the expertise and level of service
rendered.  Something quite hard to find these days!!

Phone num  603*659-2912.

This drive is NOT a standard computer floppy drive, even though it uses the
same format as regular floppy drives.  This is a very compact unit which uses
a ribbon cable for all power and control functions, similar to what you might
find in a laptop.  I may even be that a laptop floppy would be the cheapest
replacement possible.

Good Luck!

Valentin Guillen


