Steve G. wrote:

> I don't have a clue where to start on this.  I want to get an X-win terminal
> program for my NT box, and be able to run X on my linux box from NT.  I have
> a utility called X-Win32, which I'm not having very much luck with, and am
> curious if anyone else out there has done this with their alpha box, and if
> so, what terminal program are you using?

Maybe I am not clueing in to what you are after, but I think you have everything that you need. 

From your NT box, fire up X-WIN32 and then fire up a telnet program, the one that comes will NT will work, it's ugly, but it works. Telnet into your linux box and log in. Issue the command "export DISPLAY=<NT's IP Address here>:0.0" , (no quotes, no brackets) and then run something that will export X graphics, like "xclock &"  or "xterm &". The resulting windows will open on your NT box.

Hope this helps,

Norm



