Software RAID is a pain. I tried it once with limited success.  Did not
offer me what I wanted from a RAID system.  What kind of drives do you have?
This sounds to me more like a kernel problem than a RAID problem.  Make sure
in your kernel under AIC7xxx, the option for commands per LUN is NOT set to
override the driver defaults.  They might be getting overflowed if they are
older drives.  Usually the reset delay doesn't need to be touched when
you're talking about hard drives, but this might be something to look into
with that trying harder error your getting.  Dunno about that one.

Good luck!

Regards,

Steve
