That's not true. The AlphaClient doesn't "emu some x86 instructions".
RC5 is heavily based on the rotate-instruction which the alpha-cpu
doesn't have, but it's not an x86-instruction. rotl exists on many
other cpus too.

I tried to make a faster RC5-implementation, but I didn't really
succeed :(

In ftp://ftp.amazing.ch/pub/rc5 you can find my code. One is
a little bit faster than the dcti-client, but only by 10% or so.

The others are a different approach, but currently it's slower
and I don't find more optimizations. Maybe some axp-asm-guru can
look at it and teach me some tricks???

Mainly I don't have enough registers and memory/cache is too slow
(waiting for 21264...)


