The TGA is not a bad video option; the problem is that the X server (and
new fbcon code) aren't accelerated for it; they treat it like a plain dumb
framebuffer device.  With a properly optimized display driver, the TGA
could probably perform 100-fold over how it does now.  But even then, the
TGA itself is another piece of "has-been" technology.  I'd recommend the
TGA for people who have fun hacking; that's why I kept mine, at least.  But
for people who want reasonable video, trade it for an S3 or Matrox.

