> I screwed up the system when playing around with the time and
> dates.
> 
> I get an NVRAM error saying that there is a problem with the date and
> time, when change the date, it won't be accepted by the system. Is
> there a jumper, were I can reset the CMOS?
I did have the same problem when I put the date to 1-1-2000 in Linux and
then rebooted (on a XL233). Apparently this is a serious Milennium problem
cause you are thrown in a loop and cannot come out.

I went back to the shop, where they knew about the problem: an old chip. I
got a free new one and the ARC works fine now (even in 2000 :-)
Look for a chip in a socket with "REAL TIME" on it there's your
troublemaker.

Cheers,
Peter





