	Randy Carpenter (rcarpen@celt.network1.net) wrote:
	>If I try the tulip driver, it works for about 30 seconds then
happily
	>switches to 100Mbit, even though I am plugged into a 10Mbit
hub.    Does
	>anyone know what driver will work?  Maybe a later version of
tulip.c ?
	>the other alpha I have is a AS200, so I need to do the kernel
compile on
	>this machine (slow)  So, I would like to get an answer as to
which driver
	>to try before I try to compile it.

	get tulip.c 0.89 from cesdis.gsfc.nasa.gov. this works with
every 
	version of the tulip card i've found.
	you can still get the bouncing 10/100 behaviour, but if that
occurs you can
	tie it down (if you're loading it as a module) with something
like the following
	in /etc/conf.modules
	alias eth0 tulip
	options tulip options=1 debug=3

	Look in the source code for what all the options mean. IIRC
there's 1-16 which
	are for all imaginable 10/100 full/half duplex combinations plus
autodetect. 
	debugging levels go from the sublime to the 'fill a disk in half
an hour' level...

	cheers
	john



