Egads!  A delay loop on a multitasking system!

What you want to do is not difficult.

This will provide some instant enilghtenment and gratificaion:

Unix Programming FAQ
http://www.cis.ohio-state.edu/text/faq/usenet/unix-faq/programmer/faq/faq.html

For the parallel port, there are Linux HOWTO's on the subject.  Search for
the Linux Documentation Project.

For Unix programming in general, run (don't walk) out and buy W. Richard
Steven's books on the topic.  IIRC, Advanced Programming In The Unix
Environment is the title of the one you want to buy right away.  He also
has excellent books on network programming.

One last word of advice: Writing setuid programs is not for the novice
if security is a concern at all.

Regards,

Jeff

