OK, the hard drive originally supplied in these were 340MB, 2.5" SCSI
drives from Toshiba.
These are effectively unavailable nowadays.
Most people are sticking in a 2.5" IDE drive meant for a notebook computer.
Virtually all models/makes work. The big catch is that the cable for this
is a very fine pitched 44 line cable which plugs into the motherboard on a
header directly below the back of the drive. Not a commonly available part.
We make on ( part number FC530) which is designed for this. Contact me
privately if details are needed.


