Many people seem to be reading more into my statments than I said.  I am
not expecting super performance from the AS200.  I understand all too
well the issues involved with processor, memory bus, and motherboard
design.

I am not trying to compare the Intel performance to the Alpha
performance, I am just using as a guide to get some idea what the
performance range is.  It just did not seem to me that the Alpha is not
performing as well as I expected it to.  I have now received ONE
response that targeted my musings.  One person ( sorry, I forgot your
name and delete the message :( ), pointed out that the RC5 key-cracker
depends heavly on bit-rotates.  This is function that some of the Intel
processors have in hardware that gives them a performance boost that the
Alpha does not share.  The alpha has to do this function with several
instructions, so of course it suffers in the key-rate.

I was more interested in what other people were seeing in keyrates on
these machines, because I was not sure I had mine set up correctly.

-John


