>>> Daniel Stringfield said:
> On Tue, 27 Oct 1998, Wes Bauske wrote:
> 
> > I thought the srm based systems could support both srm
> > and ARC? There has been lots of discussion about switching
> > back and forth between them on this list. I use ARC and
> > AlphaBios on my systems.
> 
> I haven't been able to have any MILO boot this machine.  So the AlphaBIOS
> is useless.

Some machines have had no MILO developed for them; chief among the reasons
is lack of appropriate PALcode to manage their particular hardware (EISA
bus, full ECC, multiple CPUs, multiple PCI busses). So for those platforms,
SRM is the only possible way to boot LINUX, even though an AlphaBIOS may
exist.

--Jay++

