You can do a CD -> CDR copy if both drives are SCSI.  It is possible and it
has been done with IDE CDs, but you take the chance of running into buffer
underruns.  IDE still is not as fast as SCSI.

As I was speaking to someone in private, xcdroast seems to work the best.
There is just the matter of a little fix up in shared memory.  If you can
adjust the size of it for the Alpha, xcdroast works great.  We use it for
the Yamaha 4x2x6.  The only thing I'm not sure about and have yet to try is
rewriteables.  I'm not sure if xcdroast supports them.

If anyone has any information on CD-RW post to the list.

Kevin


