Start with "Create New Variable Set", or whatever its the name of
this menu entry, and respond like you would be installing NT (picking
up locations and the like).  Once you have a skeleton in place
edit entries for Linux.  Besides on Ruffian you can use "shortcuts"
like "A:\" or "C:\".  I do not even try to memorize all details but
this works for me every time.

