Well, first of all, some people actually TYPE URLs in once in a while, so
while the "www" prefix is common, it is certainly unnecessary.
Why not it keep it short:
axplinux.org for example.
You CAN always have an alias to it.
When you register the domain you are grabbing the latter parts, and the www
or ftp or other prefixes are coming as what you can use with it.


