>
> However "alpha" has always made visions of pre-release software dance in my
> head. Why DEC EVER chose that stupid name I'll never know..
> Besides, if you ARE an Alpha user you will know ( at least I figure that).

I think the "Alpha" name was chosen before the idea of vendors doing mass 
releases of their alpha and beta code to people caught on.  I think at that
time vendors only sent out beta code anyway.

Alpha is the first letter of the Greek alphabet.  And the Alpha Architecture
Reference Manual uses the letter in a couple of spots.  I think the designers
were shooting for the name as the first successor to the VAX or the first
64bit CPU...?

I'll worry when Intel tries to design the Omega...

Alan


