 fixed
somewhere inbetween your two versions. Due to these bugfixes some routine=
s
(like sqrt) got slower. You should use the newer glibc if you depend on y=
our
results.
There are two well optimized libs that provide parts of the libm, namely =
libffm
and libfm, maintained by K. Goto and J. Wesner. Check the web for these i=
f you
want some real speed improvements.

