> Greg Lindahl wrote:
> 
> > > [root@helix01 /root]# cat /proc/kmsg
> > > <sc 49(140f3bc70,40,8)>
> >
> > Hm, that's right, unimplemented system calls do not have newlines
> > after them. So if there were enough, that would cause memory
> > corruption downstream in syslogd.
> >
> > So let's make a patch for syslogd which inserts a newline if
> > the buffer is growing too close to the limit.
